=== /// Twice a number.
fn twice(x: Float) -> Float {
    timer(x * 2)
}
twice(2.0) ===
--- messages ---
error[Z0110]: `timer` is allowed only in a script, not inside the function `twice`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:5
  |
3 |     timer(x * 2)
  |     ^^^^^ reads or writes outside the arguments
  |
  = help: a function's result depends on its arguments alone, so it may be cached; time the call of the function in the script: `timer(f(x))`
[exit 1]

=== timer() ===
